WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.720
If the temperature outside changes
by half a degree,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.160
you won't even feel it.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.760
Such a small change is almost
imperceptible to human senses.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.120
But half a degree of global
temperature change could be

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.920
little short of the end of the world
we recognise.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.320
Or at least the world humanity has
inhabited for the last few millennia.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.080
In 2015, governments agreed a deal
in Paris to stop global warming

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.240
rising past 2 degrees and to
try to keep it below 1.5 degrees.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.760
So what's in half a degree?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.080
At 1.5 degrees,
there would still be some

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.320
precious rainforests, polar bears
and coral reefs on planet Earth,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.080
albeit seriously diminished.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.760
Sea levels would rise,
but relatively slowly,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.600
so major cities like London, Jakarta
and Mumbai have a better chance of

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.480
continuing life as normal.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.040
Drought and flooding would be at
a level where food production

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.080
can keep up with population growth.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.000
Millions of extra climate
refugees could stay at home

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.040
and others could avoid starvation.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.280
Getting to this world isn't
impossible, it means cutting

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.960
greenhouse gas emissions
by half within a decade

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.560
And then being carbon neutral
by mid-century.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.200
So we'd be closing
coal power stations instead of

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.480
building new ones

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.720
and every car would be electric.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.720
We'd be restoring forests
instead of cutting them down,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.360
and even aircraft
would be carbon neutral.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.080
It's not impossible,
but it is unlikely.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.520
The fossil fuels lobby is powerful.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.200
Some heads of state even deny
the reality of climate change.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.600
Transforming the global energy system
will take time,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.840
and trillions
of dollars of investment.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.600
But it's also an opportunity.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.160
So if we're too slow and
instead of 1.5, we get the extra

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.400
half degree - what then?

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.960
According to the latest IPCC report,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.720
in a world two degrees warmer,
you'd go diving in the tropical seas

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.800
but the flourishing
coral reefs are gone.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.720
Instead, you would likely see a
graveyard of rubble and algae.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.360
Back on land, heatwaves
are becoming increasingly deadly,

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.880
with approximately 65 million
extra people exposed to

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.040
exceptional heatwaves each year.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.120
Imagine yourself at the North Pole,
but all you see is open water.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.240
The polar bears are gone

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.960
along with the sea ice that
used to be their home.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.320
You take a boat to the edge of
Greenland, but that frozen wasteland

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.520
is thawing.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.320
Huge meltwater rivers thunder into
the ocean, where they add to the

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.080
rising sea levels that are beginning
to flood the world's coastlines.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.800
Take a trip to Miami,
Mumbai or Melbourne

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.560
and you'll probably need a boat.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.480
Faced with the rising seas,
10 million people could be forced

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.960
to pack up and move.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.720
Global harvests would also suffer,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.760
and in developing
countries especially

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.080
the number of people experiencing
water scarcity doubles.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.360
This would be a world of increasing
poverty and human misery.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.240
All for what? For half a degree.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.600
And for a few more years
of coal smoke stacks

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.280
and oil industry profits.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.680
The choice is ours, but not for long.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.480
Every bit of warming, every year,
every choice matters.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.520
But like a desert mirage,
the 1.5 degree world is receding

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.960
into the distance
with every year we delay.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.880
If carbon emissions keep growing for
decades to come,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.080
then even two degrees looks hopeful.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.120
That's a world - a darker world -
of flood, fire and conflict

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.320
that we can barely even imagine.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.920
We can still choose

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.400
that half a degree window
between unsettling dream

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.360
and full-blown nightmare.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.080
But it's closing fast.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.800
Thanks for watching. Don't forget to subscribe

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.500
and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.520
See you again soon.

